{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary","id":872222,"title":"Legendary?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T02:06:33-07:00","id":872222,"title":"Legendary?","content":"There have been some questions about introducing Epic Level/<i>Legendary</i> Changelings capable of confronting the True Fae head on. This made me wonder which mythical characters or historical figures could be introduced as Epic Changelings?<br /> <br /> Here are some suggestions:<br /> <br /> <i>King Arthur</i> Draconic Fairest Monarch of the Summer Court in Britain.<br /> <br /> <i>Merlin </i>Wizened Oracle and the Grand Vizier in Britain.<br /> <br /> <i>Edgar Allen Poe</i> as monarch of the Autumn Court<i>...(idea for his story) </i>He started as a fae touched, who gained the fairest seeming in his quest to rescue his wife Eleanor from a True who ruled a kingdom in the sea.. As such.. I see her as having the Nix kith. The Edgar Allen Poe who died in drunken poverty was Poe's Fetch.<br /> <br /> <i>Jack the Ripper</i> as Razorhand Darkling of Autumn Court... They never caught him, because he had been whisked away to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <i>Vasilisa the Brave</i> as fairest seeming (I am in Beijing, China so can't read Google documents of kiths) of the Day Court.<br /> <br /> <i>Koshchei the Deathless</i> as Giantkin Oger of Day Court<br /> <br /> <i>Rasputin</i> as Darkling of the Night Court.<br /> <br /> As why they would still be alive.... I can see Arthur gaining immortality from drinking from the Holy Grail, Koshchei and Vasilisa from a pact made with a True Fae (Baba Yaga), Poe Potentially using a contract or pledge with death/ True Fae to gain immortality.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:03:08-07:00","id":872327,"title":"","content":"I am so on with this. I wouldn't say they are exactly powerful as True Fae, but if True Fae was on Earth they could go toe to toe with them, unless True Fae was really powerful ( like Baba Yaga).<br /> <br /> Aside from deal with True Fae, they could become immortal thanks to their lives becoming legend. That is alongside their great experience and number of Contracts, one of their greatest assets-they are able to derive giant amounts of glamour from all adaptations of their stories ( maker's emotions, emotions of watchers...). Today, they mostly spend their time in hedge, planning and waiting for who knows what. They must be careful, or they risk becoming True Fae themselves.<br /> <br /> King Arthur's father traded him to True Fae in return for help in fight, despite Merlin's warming. When Arthur returned,just in time to save Britain from itself, he managed to merge with his Fetch and unite both humans and changelings. With Merlin's help he managed to pay debt he owed to his Keeper, Lady of the Lake, and in return he got freedom and was granted sanctuarity from her, to rest till his people need him. Here he is cared for by his half sister Morgana, the Nightsinger-Witchtooth Darkling. I wouldn't say he got immortality from Holy Grail, though.<br /> <br /> Lady of the Lake owed Merlin favor, which he used to gain Excalibur, one of her props. Her loyalist, Elemental ( water) Witchtooth Nimue, imprisioned him in tree deep in Hedge.<br /> Great idea for Edgar Allan Poe. Same for jack the Ripper.<br /> <br /> Vasilisa would be Flamesiren, thanks to her association with fire. Maybe even Graveweight, due to whole speaking to skull bit. She is aided by her doll. Some say it is Token, others claim it is her mother, Manikin. Vasilisa has made her home in the Hedge, decorating it with skulls of her greatest friends and enemies. She is courtless, though some say she founded court of her own long ago (I have my homebrewn court of hers) and some whisper that she is Loyalist, working for Baba Yaga. She has Contracts of Day, Night and Sun, and some say that 5 dot on Contract allows her to summon those elements to fight for her. She is solitary, and talks only with Tsarevich Ivan.<br /> <br /> Koschei seems more like Graveweight to me. He is also probably some sort of privateer.<br /> <br /> rasputin is one of younger members ( and such least powerful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:17:04-07:00","id":872340,"title":"","content":"Wyrd 10 changelings can easily be immortal in 2e. You can also achieve this at Wyrd 5+ with a one-dot merit that doubles your Wyrd for the purposes of longevity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:34:49-07:00","id":872549,"title":"","content":"Yeah, at wyrd 10, its been hinted at that your powerful enough to go toe to toe with a True Fae's earthly manifestation, you've achieved immortality, if you drop your mask and embrace the wyrd, you can have wicked dice pools and amazing power.<br /> <br /> Example a dice pool of 10 + Skill (up to 10) + Attribute (up to 10) + 10 automatic success + up to 10 dice from Embrace the Wyrd + Extra dice for each glamour spent + for some kiths getting their Wyrd as a bonus to the Skill roll (like a larcenist who spends a point of glamour to boost subtlefudge by wyrd dots) + other magic tricks or willpower to boost the roll = an enormous dice pool.<br /> <br /> Even by its self Embrace the Wyrd is wickedly good at 10 wyrd as you get 10 dice that can be used for anything you choose, + what ever glamour you choose to spend on it.<br /> <br /> That's easily enough to give pause to just about any supernatural being, including Vampire Elders, Master Mages (not archmages), Mummies, Werewolf Alphas, ect..., not just True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T02:18:07-07:00","id":872969,"title":"","content":"Here are some more ideas.<br /> <br /> <i>Robin Hood </i>Darkling Larcenist.. Contrary to the popular tale of Robin Hood being a heroic figure who robbed from the tick to give to the poor, the real Robin Hood was a well born bandit who stole from everyone and gave to himself. I think <i>Changeling: the Lost </i>particularly the Dark Ages edition should explore the historical reality.<br /> <br /> <i>The Pied Piper </i>Darkling (Am in Beijing, China right now so I can't look up the kith that has his power). A psychopath during his mortal life, he gained infamy as a changeling racketeer who kidnapped over a hundred mortal children and sold them to the True Fae... He is now on all Changeling courts equivalent of a red list and a kill on sight order given by all monarchs.<br /> <br /> <i>Hansel (Oger Gristlegrinder) </i>and <i>Gretel</i> (<i>Darkling Witchtooth)</i>. This sibling duo serves the Autumn Court in Germany as witchhunters who hunt down Autumn Courtier criminals and any supernatural that threatens the Changeling German kingdoms.<br /> <br /> <i>Snow White</i> Fairest Bright One, Winter Courtier, and High Duchess of the Duchy of the Ice-Bound Heart in Germany. She has skin as white as snow, rose red lips, and a heart as black as coal. In the original myth, Snow White executed her step mother by forcing her to dance in burning iron hot shodden shoes, so this made sense ot me.<br /> <br /> <i>Little Red Riding Hood </i>Hunter Heart Beast (Wolf) Seeming a huntress so terrifying that even Huntsmen are terrified of her.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T02:33:29-07:00","id":872974,"title":"","content":"Edgar Allen Poe's story has developed a bit more in my mind. He was contacted by an emissionary (A loyalist or hobgoblin) of a rival True Fae of the Sea King who revealed that his bride Eleanor who had died was really a Fetch and Eleanor was in the clutches of the Sea King. After entering the Hedge and surving it's many dangers, Poe came to the Sea King's domain and confronted him. The Sea King was very amused by this fae-touched who demanded his bride back, and intruiged enough, that he said he would let he and his bride leave free if Poe could survive the horrific challenges the Sea King gave him. Drawing on his skill as a writer, Poe was able to defeat and even kill the many huntsmen the Sea King sent after him and even solve the complex puzzles. In doing so, Poe gained the Author kith. He and Eleanor returned to the mortal world in time to make his fetches funeral.<br /> <br /> Poe is currently one of the most powerful and respected Autumn Monarchs in the Southern United States. Despite being over a hundred years old, his mask and mien have the appearance of a man in his early twenties, leading some to whisper that he gained immortality through a pledge made with one of the True Fae or Death, itself. He is very old fashioned in his manners and perspective, despising modern technology. He refuses to use a computer or ride an automobile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T02:42:50-07:00","id":872978,"title":"","content":"I am one of those fan's who hope that a changeling's blessing can evolve around wyrd seven. I actually think the kith blessing should evolve twice, at wyrds seven and ten.<br /> <br /> Here are some ideas.<br /> <br /> At wyrd seven, a <i>razorhand</i> can create edged weapons that automatically do peircing and aggravated damage from any part of their body (Jack the Ripper favores surgical tools). They can also rapid fire these weapons as multiple projectiles at a target, becoming living ratchett guns. At wyrd 10, they ignore armor bonuses and control the type of damage they do.<br /> <br /> At wyrd seven, a <i>Witchtooth</i> can curse a target with an appearance so groteque that people will automatically attack the target (the target is basically cursed with disquiet) or give a target an illness that can not be cured by nonmagical means. They can also fly through the air like a ghost. At wyrd 10. they can curse whole communities or unleash devastating plagues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:41:23-07:00","id":873557,"title":"","content":"Wait, but at Wyrd 10, doesn't Clarity start dropping so fast that you are basically guaranteed to hit Clarity 1 at some point, walk into the Hedge and become a True Fae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:46:11-07:00","id":873562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary?p=872978#post872978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think the kith blessing should evolve twice, at wyrds seven and ten.<br /> <br /> Here are some ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing things beyond the scope of kith blessings here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary?p=873557#post873557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, but at Wyrd 10, doesn't Clarity start dropping so fast that you are basically guaranteed to hit Clarity 1 at some point, walk into the Hedge and become a True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> That <i>can only start to happen </i>at Wyrd 10; saying that it <i>happens at </i>Wyrd 10 is like saying getting a new car inevitably leads to a head-on collision in downtown Los Angeles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T00:07:30-07:00","id":873568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary?p=873562#post873562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> That <i>can only start to happen </i>at Wyrd 10; saying that it <i>happens at </i>Wyrd 10 is like saying getting a new car inevitably leads to a head-on collision in downtown Los Angeles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, i think it's a bit more of a correlation than that. Everything I've heard has told me that the higher your Wyrd gets, the closer you are to becoming like them. It might have even been their goal in the first place on some level. You can spend a lot of time making sure you don't slip, but the problem will always be waiting for you to let your guard down. It's not like a car where you can control it with a little training. It's more like wielding a double-bladed lightsaber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T00:08:48-07:00","id":873570,"title":"","content":"but yeah, you're right, it's not guaranteed. But it just seems easier to try to stay at Wyrd 9 and compensate for the rest with entitlements and cleverness","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T00:36:24-07:00","id":873582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary?p=873568#post873568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything I've heard</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal mechanic you're referencing was in the last Changeling 1e book I finished. It is by no means difficult to fall down the slippery slope of spending all your time in circumstances that allow you to raise your Wyrd and lower your Clarity until the Arcadian invitation arrives in the mail one day, but Wyrd 10 is a prerequisite rather than a cause of Becoming Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T01:59:34-07:00","id":873612,"title":"","content":"I am in Beijing, so I can't look at the google documents. Are there ways a characters court mantle or entitlement protect your clarity? I think it would be fun to read a RPG file that focused on epic/ legendary fae and the potential Gehenna/ Raganorak level threats they have to deal with. I read and liked the plot line focused on in Changeling 1e <i>Equinox Road </i>(rescuing a kidnapped motley crewmate)<i>,</i> but felt it would have suited a Fae-touched character much better. Partly, this was my understadning that high wyrd and court mantle changelings were more noticeable than weaker changelings. Therefore, the concept of the epic level motley crew sneaking in and escaping didn't seem to fit that much with the theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T02:08:39-07:00","id":873615,"title":"","content":"Along with your kith blessing evolving, I also think you seeming blessing should evolve. As I understand it, your seeming is how you made your identity your own again. It makes sense that as your wyrd evolves through your choices and actions, your seeming would also evolve and become more obvious too.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s my idea for how the fairest seeming evolves.<br /> Wyrd 6, the fairest gets a +1 in all manipulate, persuasion, presence, and socialize rolls.<br /> Wyrd 7: The characters is immune to all penalties in appearance <i>(they don\u2019t suffer from bad B.O., they can walk through a puddle of mud and not get a speck of dirt on their shoes or clothes, and they don\u2019t need to spend hours in front of the mirror grooming themselves)</i> and all social difficulties are halved.<br /> Wyrd 8: all difficulties in persuasion, presence, and seduction are reduced to zero. When a character succeeds in any of these actions, they can give a target the swoon and inspired conditions, or the swoon and infatuated conditions, or the swoon and wanton conditions, though no more then two conditions at once.<br /> Wyrd 9: The character is immune to all fear affects and all attempts to get the fairest to betray their allies or friends fail.<br /> Wyrd 10: The Fairest and his allies can stand up to the most terrifying of True Fae and be unafraid. The Fairest can give his allies the same immunity to fear affects and betrayal that they have. They also get a +3 in finding their opponents weak point. The True Fae suffers a -5 penalty in laying a blow on the fairest or their allies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T04:13:27-07:00","id":873658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/872222-legendary?p=873557#post873557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, but at Wyrd 10, doesn't Clarity start dropping so fast that you are basically guaranteed to hit Clarity 1 at some point, walk into the Hedge and become a True Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div> That possibility was in two separate rules hacks, in two different books in fact. <br /> , <br /> In the first, the transformation is willing, both in and out of character, although the character doesn't have to realize they want to be a true fae, they just have to want to be a true fae.<br /> <br /> In the second, it's not willing, but in that setting hack wyrd isn't something you spend points on but rack up like credit card debt, and true fae hood is the equivalent of bankruptcy. <br /> <br /> So if you have to spend exp on wyrd, it's safe to say you're ST isn't using the second rules hack, and if it's the first, well first of all getting wyrd ten is a choice, as is the transformation to true fae, so the player has to make multiple decisions to get his character there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:04:46-07:00","id":874356,"title":"","content":"Had some more ideas for literary characters who could be converted into Changelings.<br /> <br /> <i>Alice Liddell </i>Moonborn Fairest (not sure which court) Alice DID in fact fall down the rabbit hole, where she met the White Rabbit (Chatelain Beast seeming), Chesire Cat (Moonborn Beast seeming), Madhatter and March Hare (Moonborn Wizened and Beast seemings) and Oger twins, Tweedle Dumb and Tweedle Dee. She rescued them from the True Fae <i>Queen of Hearts</i> and killed her Huntsman, <i>Jabberwokie</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}